WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.169
CTE stands for Career Technical Education

2
00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.755
and it differs from a traditional academic teaching credential

3
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:07.465
 in several ways.

4
00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:10.135
A CTE credential authorizes you to teach

5
00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:12.012
within a specific subject area,

6
00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.346
because you have a depth

7
00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.639
and breadth of experience

8
00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.058
as a working professional
in that field.

9
00:00:17.058 --> 00:00:18.685
The courses that you would then be eligible

10
00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.229
to teach with the CTE would be designated as

11
00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:25.108
Career Technical, Vocational, or Trade courses

12
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.652
by the district in which you get hired.

13
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:30.488
Some basic requirements to earn a CTE credential

14
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:32.449
in arts/media/entertainment include:

15
00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:34.200
having a high school diploma

16
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.786
and verification from employers

17
00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.748
that you have at least three years of work experience

18
00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:42.917
directly related to arts, media, and entertainment.

19
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:46.963
That's at least 1000 hours each year for three years.

20
00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:48.715
What's unique about this credential is

21
00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.758
you don't have to enroll

22
00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:51.843
in a multi-year
university program.

23
00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:53.511
You can pursue it
through your county office

24
00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:56.014
of education,
university extensions,

25
00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:58.600
and other continuing education programs.

26
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.351
With a preliminary CTE,

27
00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:02.103
you can even work
towards your credential

28
00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:03.897
while you're teaching
in a classroom.

29
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.607
And typically,

30
00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:07.442
those with a CTE credential continue

31
00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:08.985
to pursue their arts practice

32
00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:11.821
and stay active
in their creative field.

33
00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:13.990
There are other details
outlined in this website,

34
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.785
but the most important point
to remember is that

35
00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:20.038
your experience, your knowledge, insight,

36
00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:21.873
and skills from working
in the field of arts,

37
00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:24.125
media, and entertainment
are requirements

38
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:25.710
for earning that CTE credential,

39
00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.796
and they're also what distinguish you and

40
00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:29.714
make you eligible to teach.
